From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:55:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mark the decrypted block size as used outside its assertion

The decrypting transport's ReadBlock() keeps the byte count that
Process() returns only for D_ASSERT() to compare against the block it
read, so in a release build, where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, the
local is unused and -Wunused-variable says so. A (void) cast after the
assertion marks it used, the way the engine already treats locals that
only an assertion reads.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.
---
 src/duckdb/extension/parquet/parquet_crypto.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/extension/parquet/parquet_crypto.cpp b/src/duckdb/extension/parquet/parquet_crypto.cpp
index aebc50fc1a..f558eeb010 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/extension/parquet/parquet_crypto.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/extension/parquet/parquet_crypto.cpp
@@ -364,6 +364,7 @@ private:
 		// Decrypt directly into the destination only after checking that the whole block fits.
 		auto size = aes->Process(read_buffer + ParquetCrypto::BLOCK_SIZE, read_buffer_size, buf, buffer_size);
 		D_ASSERT(size == read_buffer_size);
+		(void)size;
 		read_buffer_offset = 0;
 	}
 
